<title>FINLAND: OKOBANK UP SHARPLY AFTER Q1 RESULT.</title>
<headline>OKOBANK UP SHARPLY AFTER Q1 RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish bank OKOBANK rose sharply on Tuesday after it reported first quarter operating profits after credit losses up 36 percent on the same period last year, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The result was a positive surprise. They made their profits on core banking business,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>At 1545/1345 GMT, OKOBANK traded at 74.10 markka, up 6.10 markka or almost nine percent. It earlier hit 75.00 markka.</p>
<p>The 2.3 million markka volume was lively for the share.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-680 50 235</p>
